**What I found and fixed**

The filed finding reproduced exactly (0 tests across all four REPL modules; `ReplCommand`/`ReplHistory`/`ReplCompleter` constructed nowhere). Reading the code turned up something worse than dead weight — **the REPL hangs forever on EOF**: `read_line` returns `Ok(0)`, `run` did `continue`, so `printf 'say 1\n' | rb` spun printing `>>> ` (9.9 MB in 3 s, exit 124 under `timeout`). Fixed at src/repl/mod.rs:81.

Routing `handle_command` through `ReplCommand::parse` (deleting the duplicate table) failed3 of 10 e2e tests on first run — the shared table couldn't tell "not a command" from "unknown command", so `2 + 3` was answered `Unknown command '2 + 3'` and never evaluated. Added `NotACommand` and `MissingArgument` variants; `:load` with no argument now says `Usage: :load <filename>` again rather than calling itself unknown.

Two smaller real bugs found by the new tests: `ReplHistory::new(0)` held one entry, and `.quit` was rejected (old table stripped only `:`, `parse` strips `:` or `.`).

**Gates**: fmt pass · clippy `-D warnings` pass · `cargo test --all-targets` **785 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored** (was 734) · `rb test` 274/274 · all 6 `examples/*.rb` + both `modules/*.rb` run.

**Gate 4 I did not run**: `./rbops/verify.sh phase-033` → exit 127, `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout. I have not claimed it passes, in the report or here.

51 new tests (41 in `src/repl/`, 10 e2e in `tests/repl_test.rs`), 17 named `edge_*`, no `#[ignore]`/`allow(`. `REPORT.md` and `FINDINGS.md` written to `phases/phase-033/` with every `file:line` verified against the files — including two transcripts I had to correct after running them for real.

Six unfixed defects are filed in `FINDINGS.md` with evidence, the largest being that **the REPL cannot use a variable it just set** (`set x to 1` then `say x` → `AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'x'`), which makes it much less usable than the dead code I removed.

DONE
